\details{
The Variance-Adjusted Weighted UniFrac distance is defined as:
\deqn{\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n} L_i\frac{|P_i - Q_i|}{\sqrt{(P_i + Q_i)(2 - P_i - Q_i)}} }{\sum_{i=1}^{n} L_i\frac{P_i + Q_i}{\sqrt{(P_i + Q_i)(2 - P_i - Q_i)}} }}

Where:
\itemize{
\item \eqn{n} : The number of branches in the tree.
\item \eqn{L_i} : The length of the \eqn{i}-th branch.
\item \eqn{P_i}, \eqn{Q_i} : The proportion of the community descending from branch \eqn{i} in sample P and Q.
}
